    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (85.99) stands as the clear anchor of the LawDog lineup. Facing Whisenhunt\u2019s porous 5.60 xERA, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a massive SP-skill bump and the high-leverage protection of the #2 spot, making him the only elite-tier play on the board. **Daulton Varsho** (68.65) also earns a premium start today; while he draws a right-handed matchup, the combination of his dynamic platoon advantage against Klassen and a significant SP-skill boost makes him a much higher-value asset than his standard projections suggest. We are also leaning on **Bryce Harper** (66.64) to provide power stability against a mid-tier Gibson, C, as his superior xwOBA metrics and favorable park factors solidify his role in the heart of our order.\n\nWe faced a tight squeeze at the bottom of the active roster, with **Zack Gelof** (56.30) and **Yainer Diaz** (56.73) narrowly avoiding the bench. The most difficult exclusion was **Gleyber Torres** (38.15), who missed the cut primarily due to the stringent 40.0 floor we apply to preserve game caps; despite a favorable lead-off spot, the SP-skill penalty from facing a sub-3.30 xERA arm like Ashcraft, B rendered him a liability today. Elsewhere, we are cautious about our high-speed prospects like **Justin Crawford** (48.16); though his SB upside is theoretically critical for our build, his L/L platoon disadvantage against Gibson, C effectively neutralized his ceiling today, making him a marginal start at best.\n\nLooking ahead, we are monitoring the volatility of the bottom-tier matchups closely. **Lawrence Butler** (46.44) and **JJ Bleday** (47.33) remain in the lineup, but both are trending toward the sub-50 threshold due to severe platoon inhibitors\u2014a 13% and 14% drop, respectively. While we would typically look to rotate in depth pieces like **Brendan Donovan**, the SP-skill risk in his matchup against Harrison, L dictates that we play it safe today. Ensure we keep an eye on the official lineups, as any late movement impacting the order slots for **Jonathan Aranda** or **Masyn Winn** could shift their efficiency scores rapidly given the sensitivity of our current roster optimization.",
